      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Analgesic and anti-inflammatory activities of the aqueous and ethanol extracts of Thespesia populnea Soland. ex. Correa (Malvaceae) leaves were evaluated in animal models. Orally-administered aqueous and ethanol extracts (100, 200 and 400\u2009mg\u2009kg\u207b¹ bw) showed significant analgesic activity in chemical-, mechanical- and thermally-induced pain test models in mice. The extracts also reduced paw oedema induced by carrageenan in rats. The results obtained in this study suggest that Thespesia populnea extracts have analgesic and anti-inflammatory properties."},
